es and tips of mature canes, carrying a large cluster of pale yellow or yellow flowers. Each flower is approximately 5cm large, pale or brigh yellow, ofter with dark-reddish markings.","image":"DendrobiumHildaPoxon.jpg","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":341517,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendrobium</em> Hsinying Frosty Maree gx","entityDescription":"A medium-sized, tropical orchid with 30-40cm long, upright cane-like stems. Each stem (pseudobulb) is also a storage organ of water and nutrients. The canes are covered with alternate thin, leaf-bearing sheaths covered in dense, short black hairs. Leaves are dark green, oval or elliptic, spaced along the whole length of the canes. The plant flowers with short clusters of attractive, star-shaped white or pale green flowers with bright orange lip. Flowers are 5-6cm large, long-lasting and fragrant.","image":"DendrobiumHsinyingFrostyMaree.jpg","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":31339,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendrobium</em> Malones gx","entityDescription":"An evergreen, clump-forming, epiphytic orchid with long, cane-like pseudobulbs. Each pseudobulb is a modification of a stem, which serves as a storage of water and nutrients. Oblong, alternate leaves up to 10cm. Dark pink flowers with white-margined yellow centres are approximately 7cm across. Flowers are produced on short stems in pairs from the nodes on mature pseudobulbs.","image":"","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":132447,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendrobium</em> Margaret Thatcher gx","entityDescription":"A large-sized, tropical, evergreen orchid with long, upright, ca