ally white, sometimes cream, with a hint of pale pink.","image":"DendrobiumSunSpritegx.jpg","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":165354,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendrobium</em> Superbum gx","entityDescription":"A large-sized, epiphytic orchid with 120cm long, pendulous, cane-like, noded stems. Each new stem is enveloped with alternate leaf-sheaths along each node, carrying one bright green, glossy, deciduous leaf, 12-18cm long. Short flowering stems, carrying one 7cm large flower, appear from the nodes along mature, leafless stems in spring. The flowers are usually pale pink, but may vary from whitish to dark pink forms. Characteristic for this species is the densely hairy lip.","image":"Dendrobiumanosmum2.jpg","commonName":"unscented dendrobium","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":5432,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Dendrobium</em> <em>anosmum</em>","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":165916,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendrobium</em> Utopia gx","entityDescription":"A medium to large-sized, epiphytic orchid with long, cane-like stems. Glossy, oval-shaped leaves are alternately arranged along the nodes of the stems. Each leaf is 8-12cm long and 3cm wide. One or two fragrant flowers, 6-7cm large are carried on short flowering stems, emerging from nodes of mature canes. The flowers are bright pink-magenta, with pale, yellow/white centre.","image":"DendrobiumUtopia2.jpg","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":165104,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendrobium</em> <em>aggregatum</em>","entityDescription":"A small-sized, evergreen, epiphytic orchid. Upright, clump-forming stems (pseudobulbs) are spindle-shaped, up to 10cm long and bears one leathery, dark-green, 7-8cm long 